 ## English
 
-### Goal
+### Established research
 
-Work out what the IMX410 actually does in the fp: how ISO maps onto conversion
-gain and analog gain, what each sensor mode's parameters are, and which numbers
-the firmware confirms versus which are OTP values that still need measuring.
+The ISO/gain chain has been decompiled, including conversion gain, analog gain,
+readout and the ADC stage. The [interactive explainer](https://ijigen.github.io/fpSup/explainers/imx410-iso-gain.html)
+distinguishes firmware-confirmed behavior from OTP values that need measurement.
 
-### Proven
+The three picker tables (`0xC0BE5810`, `0xC0BE59B0`, `0xC0BE5B50`) select sensor
+modes by geometry and frame rate. The stock FHD 29.97 slot selects mode 106;
+a recorded take confirmed 106 at `0xC343B590`. The corresponding FHD 29.97
+CinemaDNG rolling-shutter result is 10.556 ms. These are specific mode results,
+not a claim that all sensor behavior is solved.
 
-- **The ISO and gain chain is fully decompiled** — conversion gain, analog gain,
-  analog readout and the ADC stage
-- The result is an [interactive explainer](https://ijigen.github.io/fpSup/) in
-  English and Traditional Chinese that **separates firmware-confirmed behaviour
-  from OTP values that still require measurement**
-- Recording geometry at `0xC37CE210` = {1936, 1090, 3244544 bytes per frame}
+**Correction:** `0xC37CE210` is a downstream geometry cache, not an authoritative
+source. The earlier `{1936, 1090, 3244544}` observation does not establish causality;
+a later take produced valid 1936×1090 DNGs while that cache was all zero.
+The geometry intervention was demonstrated in the FieldAngle record assembled
+by `FUN_c043a158`, before its derived values are calculated.
 
-### Open
+### Current implementation and remaining work
 
-> ✅ **Resolved 2026-09-10 — and the mode-index field was never needed.**
-> The mode is chosen by a table, so read the table. The picker's three arrays
-> (`0xC0BE5810` / `0xC0BE59B0` / `0xC0BE5B50`, 26 entries of 16 bytes, `+0x08`
-> the sensor mode) are laid out as *(readout geometry × frame rate)*, and the
-> FHD 29.97 slot holds **106**. **Mode 111 does not appear in any of the three.**
-> A real take reads 106 back from `0xC343B590`.
->
-> **FHD 29.97 CinemaDNG rolling shutter is 10.556 ms.** That is the number gyro
-> sup's lens profile was missing. See `../research/imx410/notes/FRAME_RATE_IS_VMAX.md`.
+Custom Sensor has a seven-axis recipe engine and limited prior recording evidence.
+The latest offline changes synchronize native bit-depth/frame-rate selections,
+correct RAW14 latching, make unknown burst capacity explicit, and package ordinary
+and debug cards through the shared builder with shutdown restoration. This build
+has not been tested on the camera or released; Fast/merged packaging is unsupported.
+
+The on-camera mode selector and conditional disabling, per-clip playback geometry,
+RAW14 gain/packing, CRCT validation and repeated power cycles remain open.
+Solvable RAW14 donors and offline tests do not establish recording readiness.
 
